      "content": "Thanks for the start. It's a bit short and a little vague, though. Can you expand this into a full formal letter? \n\nWe need to actually address the specific claim about the delayed hardware delivery. We should mention that while the delay happened, it wasn't due to gross negligence, but we're still open to talking about a credit or something similar. \n\nJust a reminder: try to keep the tone professional and don't overdo the \"concession\" language. I really don't want a letter that sounds like we're admitting fault or just saying \"we agree to everything\" because I need to keep the partner from seeing the score as being artificially inflated. Just make it a solid, substantive legal draft.",
